<title>MOROCCO: Moroccan Treasury auction raises 676.50mln dirhams.</title>
<headline>Moroccan Treasury auction raises 676.50mln dirhams.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Moroccan Treasury raised 676.50 million dirhams from its weekly treasury bill auction, Bank al-Maghrib (central bank) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Rates and amounts (in million dirhams) were accepted as follows:</p>
<p>    MATURITY	 BID	   AMOUNT	   INTEREST RATE</p>
<p>    13 weeks	  30	    30			7.5</p>
<p>    26 weeks	  30	    30			8</p>
<p>    52 weeks	 290	   290			8.5</p>
<p>    Two years	137.75	103.50		   8.8</p>
<p>    Five years	90	    90			9.5 pct</p>
<p>    10 years	 100	   100		     10.25</p>
<p>    15 years	  33	    33		     10.50 pct</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Total	   710.50	  676.50</p>
<p>Maturity date was set for March 25, 1997.</p>
<p>($1= 9.3 dirhams)</p>
<p>(( - Rabat newsroom +212-7 726518 ))</p>
</text>
